# Plain chat must not promote into slash / quick actions

**Product law:** Plain English in the composer is **plain chat**. The agent / intent planner may gather, search, name tools, and answer. It must **never** enter a slash-command pipeline or a quick-action pipeline unless the user **explicitly** chose that workflow on **this turn**.

## Explicit (keep)

- Typed slash token on this send (`SLASH_COMMANDS` — `/blast`, `/owner`, `/trace`, `/gaps`, `/understand`, `/edit`, `/fix`, `/compare`, `/slack`, `/jira`, `/teams`, `/confluence`, `/notion`, `/docs`, and aliases)
- Workflows menu insert (puts `/blast ` etc. in the composer; user then sends)
- Quick-action grid / editor command / prompt-library entry that already carries an `actionId` or slash
- Sources-card / evidence-card “run this action” buttons that already send `quickAction`

## Not explicit (never do)

- Phrase-bank matches (“If I change…”, “who owns…”, “what breaks if…”)
- Cheap intent-suggest model classifying a workflow
- Planner `execution: "silent"` / `mode: "run-workflow"` from plain text
- Confirm chips (“Want Blast Radius?” / `Run /blast` / `Just answer`)
- Sticky inherit of `[blast-radius]` / last `/blast` onto a later **plain** follow-up
- Auto-setting `composerMode: "edit"` from a change-shaped sentence when the user did not type `/edit` or `/fix`
- Auto-setting `quickAction` or slash-style `integrationProvider` just because the sentence resembles that command

## Implementation choke

On unconstrained turns (`constraint.kind === "none"`, no `quickAction`, no parsed slash, no composer edit from slash/UI):

- Do not return `silent-workflow` or `confirm-workflow`
- Do not call `shouldOfferQuickActionSuggest` / chip clarification
- Do not set `quickAction` from planner `workflow`
- Do not plan a workflow field (jobs + named tools + `codeIntent` stay)
- Named Slack/Jira/… may **prefetch** via `fetchIntegrations`; do **not** set `integrationProvider` (that is the slash single-route)

`/edit` `/fix` (or explicit composer edit) may set `composerMode: "edit"`. Plain change asks use the agent loop / `propose_patch`, never anchored-edit hijack.

File-level Blast/Trace error banners are correct **only** after an explicit command.

## Self-check

Would “If I change that missing-key response, what else should I check?” with Use-repo and no file silently enter Blast Radius? If yes, fail.
